0..47 Comment "//! A relative monad is relative to shift `-F`."
48..51 Comment "//!"
52..132 Comment "//! A unit returns a value. An extension runs a computation into a continuation."
133..136 Comment "//!"
137..212 Comment "//! The host part has definitions for the option monad. The source also has"
213..257 Comment "//! code that is polymorphic in the carrier."
258..314 Comment "//! The left unit is a second-order rule. The right unit"
315..343 Comment "//! abstracts a continuation"
344..403 Comment "//! variable. Associativity and both units form one theory."
404..407 Comment "//!"
408..445 Comment "//! - see: #2115 — `MonadRightUnit`"
446..482 Comment "//! - see: #2116 — `RelativeMonad`"
483..545 Comment "//! - cites: [Altenkirch-2015-monads_need_not_be_endofunctors]"
546..625 Comment "//! - cites: [Jiang-2025-notions_stackmanipulating_computation_relative_monads]"
